for . This answers a question by Navarro for and and partly answers it for .\n\n## Keywords\n\nSymmetric group\n\n;\n\nCharacters\n\n;\n\nPartitions--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA new estimate on complexity of binary generalized pseudostandard words (https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.05482)\nciteturn0academia17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.0 years ago; Generalized pseudostandard words were introduced by de Luca and De Luca in 2006. ... We present a counterexample to Conjecture 43 from a paper by Blondin Mass\\'e et al. that estimated the complexity of binary generalized pseudostandard words as ${\\mathcal C}(n) \\leq 4n$ for all sufficiently large $n$.\nTitle: A new estimate on complexity of binary generalized pseudostandard words\nAuthors: Lubomira Dvorakova, Josef Florian\nDate: Wed Nov 16 22:09:39 2016\n\nGeneralized pseudostandard words were introduced by de Luca and De Luca in 2006. In comparison to the palindromic and pseudopalindromic closure, only little is known about the generalized pseudopalindromic closure and the associated generalized pseudostandard words. We present a counterexample to Conjecture 43 from a paper by Blondin Mass\\'e et al. that estimated the complexity of binary generalized pseudostandard words as ${\\mathcal C}(n) \\leq 4n$ for all sufficiently large $n$. We conjecture that ${\\mathcal C}(n)<6n$ for all $n \\in \\mathbb N$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) Combinatorics of Tableau Inversions | Download on Academia (https://www.academia.edu/78468924/Combinatorics_of_Tableau_Inversions)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; For a quick specialization to rectangular tableaux of size m\u0001 × n, note that Proposi- tion 2.2 gives a maximum inversion number of Mn,...,n = n m2 . ... Notice that this is in the electronic journal of combinatorics 22(2) (2015), #P2.44 19 agreement with what Append